---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Stub from '../components/Stub.astro';
import { machines } from '../data/machines';
---
<Base title="Support · Lemus" description="Lemus plugins: user guides, the ROM folder, panel artwork, the update check, and contact." current="support">
<Stub heading="Support">
<p>What all Lemus plugins share. Each plugin's own controls are in its user guide; installing is on the <a href="/download#installing">download page</a>.</p>

<h2 id="guides" class="h3">User guides</h2>
<ul>
{machines.map((m) => <li><a href={`/${m.slug}/guide`} class="mono">{m.slug}</a>: {m.emulates}</li>)}
</ul>

<h2 id="rom" class="h3">ROM images</h2>
<p>A machine's firmware is its maker's copyrighted work, so Lemus doesn't include it. A machine with a CPU runs it from your own ROM image; its guide names the file and its SHA1. Without it, a machine marked [~] plays its voice over MIDI but nothing the CPU does; one marked [✗] doesn't run.</p>
<p>The ROM folder is <span class="path">~/Library/Application Support/Lemus/ROMs</span> on macOS and <span class="path">%APPDATA%\Lemus\ROMs</span> on Windows, shared by every Lemus plugin; each plugin can point it elsewhere, and About shows the one in use. ROMs are matched by SHA1, under any name, loose, in subfolders or in zips: MAME sets work as they are. Adding one later restores the whole machine in an open session.</p>

<h2 id="artwork" class="h3">Panel artwork</h2>
<p>Makers' logos and model names are trademarks, so their places on the panel are blank. Each plugin writes an SVG file to the ROM folder in use, if it has none, with a commented-out slot for each place; artwork in a slot, comments removed, is drawn on the panel the next time the plugin starts. An SVG in any other folder is ignored. The slot names and units are in the plugin's guide.</p>

<h2 id="updates" class="h3">Update check</h2>
<p>Once a day, while a plugin window is open, the plugin fetches one small file from lemusdev.org and sends nothing about you. When a new version is out, a window lists what changed: Download, Remind me later (again in a week) or Skip this version (until the next one). The bar shows the update until it is installed. About › Check for updates once a day turns it all off.</p>

<h2 id="mailing-list" class="h3">Mailing list</h2>
<p>The mailing list carries release announcements only. The form at the foot of each page adds an address after it is confirmed by email. The list is held by Kit, which sends the mail; every email has an unsubscribe link.</p>

<h2 id="contact" class="h3">Contact</h2>
<p><a href="mailto:hello@lemusdev.org">hello@lemusdev.org</a>. With a problem, give the plugin and version (in About), your system, your DAW and what you did. Security issues: <a href="mailto:security@lemusdev.org">security@lemusdev.org</a>.</p>
</Stub>
</Base>

<style>
.h3 { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 26px; scroll-margin-top: 16px; }
p, li { color: var(--ink2); font-size: 16px; }
p { margin: 0; max-width: 46em; }
ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; }
.mono { font-size: 15px; }
.path { font: 14px var(--mono); color: var(--ink); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
